;;;   card-disjoint-family       card of the union of a finite disjoint family = sum of the cards
;;;   zz-gcd-pos-exists, zz-gcd-pos-unique, zz-divides-le-pos, zz-gcd-scale   the positive gcd; gcd(cj, ce) = c iff (j, e) = 1
;;;   gauss-class-card, gauss-phi-sum   sum_{d | n} phi(d) = n
;;;   powers-subgroup, powers-card, element-order-divides-card, element-order-unique, order-partition
;;;                              ord(x) | card G; card G = sum_{d | card G} #{x : ord(x) = d}
;;;   finsum-cc-le-termwise, subset-card-eq, order-of-power-coprime, order-count-le-at, order-count-le,
;;;   phiset-card-pos, order-card-generator
;;;   finite-group-cyclic-criterion   LEMMA 5.44: a finite group with at most d solutions of x^d = e for every d >= 1
;;;                              is cyclic (the notes assume Abelian; the proof does not use it)
;;; LOAD WINDOW.  lo: cyclic-product (and its window), group-cosets (lagrange), inclusion-exclusion (the C sums),
;;; finsum-insert, rake-finsum-union (finsum-insert-ptwise), rake-finsum-laws (finsum-congruence-q), card-laws.
